  "title": "S3: README documents plug-and-play executor rows (Codex and claude:<tier>)",
  "spec": "Goal T-1334. Docs only, README.md section \"Executors and routing\" (locate by heading; near README.md:278). Add a subsection \"Adding or removing models\" covering, in plain prose plus one TOML example each:\n- Codex model: add an [[executors]] row with provider = \"codex\", model = the id from ~/.codex/models_cache.json, roles, complexity_min/max, max_parallel, daily_budget_tasks, quota_group, weight, enabled.\n- Claude model: add an alias under [models] (e.g. opus = \"claude-opus-5-5\"), then a row with id = \"claude:<alias>\" and provider = \"claude\"; model is optional and must equal the alias value; an invalid claude row loads disabled with a reason. Routed Claude tasks run through the same path as the Claude fallback (account with headroom, other-account other-model review).\n- Headroom and limits: a claude row is only routed while some [[claude_accounts]] account has headroom; keep its max_parallel small, because [limits].max_parallel_claude_workers is not yet enforced for routed Claude executes at scheduler level (follow-up in .orchestrator/plan.md).\n- Running without Codex: set enabled = false on every codex row; [codex].on_exhausted still governs the legacy fallback.\n- Review rule: a reviewer never runs the model that executed the task (compared by model id).\nAccuracy check: every field and behaviour named must exist in orchestrator/pool.py, executor.py and daemon.py on this branch; read them, do not invent options. No code changes.",
